==Battleground==
*1 [[Dark Otter]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gory Groom]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Gorilliam]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
**3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
**5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.33 seconds<sup>2f~10f</sup>.
**5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**5 [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since all of the enemies in this stage are close-ranged, it is highly recommended to bring meatshields. At the beginning of the battle, a Dark Otter will spawn, which may seem scary, but a few Doge Darks will come in. They are easy to deal with and drop loads of money, so use that to your advantage to save up cash and send out a heavy unit. If you have no heavy units, rangers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] will help. Anti-Dark units are helpful as well even if they have low range.

==Trivia==
*The name of this stage is a reference to the game show [[wikipedia:Family Feud|Family Feud]].

